<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $113.4 mln June 23.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $113.4 mln June 23.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $113.4 million deficit on June 23 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown:</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 23</p>
<p>Exports: $112.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $269.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $227.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $183.7 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $113.4 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.550 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.252 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $6.037 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $5.561 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $226 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
